\fs29\fsmilli14857 \cf2 \cb3 6. Where it's headed / recommended correction\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf2 \cb3 No change of direction needed. Three steps, in order:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Finish + commit E5's edge metric
\f0 \'a0(~25 min GPU). Closes the one known-open defect; either H5 survives on a non-tautological ruler or it doesn't \'97 both are publishable.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Move E3/E4 to a real LM (Pythia-160M).
\f0 \'a0This is the highest-value step and what the adversarial audit demanded: the Heap et al. control only has its intended meaning where a random model's activations\'a0
\f3\i aren't
\f0\i0 \'a0trivially reconstructable. It converts H3 from "refuted on a toy" to a real result.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Stop adding toys after that.
\f0 \'a0The marginal information from another synthetic experiment is low; the active-inference selector already showed its blind spot here (it ranks already-answered questions highly because EIG models outcome uncertainty, not redundancy).\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

